Isotope: window controls on the left of the header bar, as round buttons.

What: a new CosmicTk key, `window_controls_left` (bool, false when the key is
not set, so upstream's layout stays the default). When it is true, the header
bar packs close, minimize and maximize, in that order, at the very start
instead of at the end, as round 12 px buttons filled with the theme's neutral
button colour, outlined with the divider colour, that show their glyph only
under the pointer. Changes src/config/mod.rs (the field, its default, a
`config::window_controls_left()` getter) and src/widget/header_bar.rs.

Why: Isotope's look puts the window buttons on the left (the "lights" of
docs/superpowers/specs/assets/isotope-look/mock.html), and Isotope ships
/usr/share/cosmic/com.system76.CosmicTk/v1/window_controls_left = true. Every
COSMIC app draws its header with this widget, and cosmic-comp draws the
server-side title bars with it (src/shell/element/window.rs,
DefaultDecorations), so one patch covers apps and SSD windows. A user turns it
off with `false` in ~/.config/cosmic/com.system76.CosmicTk/v1/window_controls_left.

Made against libcosmic 430f3d48a97d (COSMIC epoch-1.11.0). src/config/mod.rs
and src/widget/header_bar.rs are the same at d922ac380134 (cosmic-comp) and
8cb10bf6e24b (cosmic-workspaces), and the patch applies to all three.

